## Apply final-review hardenings before port

Context:
Applied the two actionable final-review hardenings requested for branch/worktree
`0.8.1` before porting: keep translator-compatible predicate-IN aliases accepted
by the validator, and tighten specialized relationship-UNION validation so
non-specialized UNION shapes fail at capability validation time (instead of
failing later with unrelated mapping errors). Work was done test-first with
explicit RED then GREEN verification.

Changes:

1. `tests/back/core/w3c/sparql/test_sparql_capability_validator.py`
   Added positive tests for `FILTER(?predicate|?p|?pred IN (...))` URI lists and
   added negative tests proving non-specialized UNION variants are rejected with
   the `UNION` capability error.
2. `tests/back/core/w3c/sparql/test_sparql_translator_units.py`
   Added public-translator positive tests for `predicate/p/pred` IN aliases and
   added negative tests proving unsupported non-specialized UNION shapes raise
   capability `ValidationError` containing `UNION`.
3. `src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlCapabilityValidator.py`
   Extended allowed IN-variable aliases to `predicate`, `p`, and `pred`; carried
   projected SELECT variables through validation traversal; and tightened UNION
   acceptance to the translator-compatible specialized shape only
   (`SELECT ?subject ?predicate ?object` plus branch variable naming
   `?subject ... ?object` with `BIND(... AS ?predicate)`).
4. `src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlTranslator.py`
   Tightened `_is_specialized_relationship_union_query` to require exact branch
   variable naming (`subject`, `object`) in addition to existing projected
   variables and predicate constraints, keeping validator and translator aligned.

